---
/**
 * EnergyEconomyBench — the chapter's ONE idea made manipulable: metabolism is an
 * energy economy. Thermodynamically unfavorable reactions don't happen on their own;
 * the cell DRIVES them by coupling to ATP hydrolysis, and its spending is gated by
 * energy charge. Three benches:
 *   1. Couple it      — add an uphill reaction's ΔG°' to ATP's −30.5 and watch the
 *                       sum (and K'eq) flip from "won't go" to spontaneous.
 *   2. Rank the donors — drag a phosphoryl group down the transfer-potential ladder;
 *                        the cell can only push phosphate downhill (PEP→ADP→glucose).
 *   3. Read the battery — an energy-charge gauge: EC = (ATP + ½ADP)/(ATP+ADP+AMP).
 *                        Drop ATP and AMP rises disproportionately (adenylate kinase),
 *                        redlining the needle and flipping the cell into BURN mode.
 * Self-contained vanilla-TS Astro island. No libraries, no props. Original — every
 * number is computed from the equations, nothing is AI-drawn.
 */
---

<figure class="eeb card" data-eeb>
  <figcaption class="eeb-head">The Energy Economy Bench — coupling, currency, and the cell's battery<span class="eeb-chip">⚙ original · interactive</span></figcaption>

  <div class="eeb-grid">
    <!-- MODULE 1 — Couple it -->
    <section class="eeb-mod">
      <h3 class="eeb-modh">Couple it: ATP pays for the uphill climb</h3>
      <svg class="eeb-svg eeb-svg-hill" viewBox="0 0 260 150" role="img" data-svg="hill" aria-label="Two wagons on a hill showing reaction coupling"></svg>

      <div class="eeb-ctl">
      <label class="eeb-slabel"><span>Uphill reaction A → B: ΔG°' = <em data-out="targetdg">+12</em> kJ/mol</span>
        <input type="range" data-in="targetdg" min="5" max="25" step="1" value="12" />
      </label>
      <label class="eeb-check">
        <input type="checkbox" data-in="couple" />
        Couple to ATP hydrolysis (−30.5 kJ/mol)
      </label>

      <dl class="eeb-readout">
        <div><dt>ΔG°' of target</dt><dd data-out="dg-target">+12.0 kJ/mol</dd></div>
        <div><dt>ΔG°' summed</dt><dd data-out="dg-sum">+12.0 kJ/mol</dd></div>
        <div><dt>K'eq (310 K)</dt><dd data-out="keq">9.5e-3</dd></div>
      </dl>
      <p class="eeb-verdict" data-out="verdict" role="status"></p>
      <p class="eeb-tip">The two reactions are linked through a shared intermediate, so their ΔG°' values simply add.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- MODULE 2 — Rank the donors -->
    <section class="eeb-mod">
      <h3 class="eeb-modh">Rank the donors: phosphate only rolls downhill</h3>
      <svg class="eeb-svg eeb-svg-ladder" viewBox="0 0 200 300" role="img" data-svg="ladder" aria-label="Phosphoryl-transfer potential ladder with a draggable phosphate token"></svg>
      <div class="eeb-ctl">
      <p class="eeb-laddermsg" data-out="laddermsg" role="status">The phosphate (orange token) starts on ATP. Drag it to another rung, or focus it and press ↓ / ↑. Which moves does the cell allow?</p>
      <div class="eeb-start" role="group" aria-label="Put the phosphate back on a starting rung">
        <span>Start the phosphate on:</span>
        <button type="button" data-start="0">PEP</button>
        <button type="button" data-start="3">ATP</button>
      </div>
      <p class="eeb-tip">Transfer potential = −ΔG°' of hydrolysis. ATP sits in the middle on purpose: high-energy donors (PEP, 1,3-BPG, creatine-P) can charge it; it in turn can phosphorylate glucose. Glucose-6-P can't pay ATP back.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- MODULE 3 — Read the battery -->
    <section class="eeb-mod">
      <h3 class="eeb-modh">Read the battery: energy charge gates spending</h3>
      <svg class="eeb-svg eeb-svg-gauge" viewBox="0 0 200 130" role="img" data-svg="gauge" aria-label="Energy charge gauge from 0 to 1"></svg>
      <div class="eeb-ctl">
      <div class="eeb-ec">Energy charge <strong data-out="ec">0.91</strong></div>
      <div class="eeb-ampk" data-out="ampk" role="status">High charge — STORE mode</div>
      <div class="eeb-modes">
        <span class="eeb-mode" data-mode="cata">🔥 catabolic · burn fuel</span>
        <span class="eeb-mode" data-mode="ana">🧱 anabolic · build</span>
      </div>
      <label class="eeb-slabel"><span>[ATP] <em data-out="atp">85</em></span><input type="range" data-in="atp" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="85" /></label>
      <label class="eeb-slabel"><span>[ADP] <em data-out="adp">12</em></span><input type="range" data-in="adp" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="12" /></label>
      <label class="eeb-slabel"><span>[AMP] <em data-out="amp">3</em></span><input type="range" data-in="amp" min="0" max="100" step="1" value="3" /></label>
      <p class="eeb-akrow" data-out="akrow" aria-live="polite"></p>
      <p class="eeb-tip">Drag ATP down and watch AMP. Adenylate kinase (2 ADP ⇌ ATP + AMP) stays near equilibrium, so as ATP is spent the leftover ADP is partly converted to AMP: AMP rises far faster, in relative terms, than ATP falls. That makes AMP the cell's sensitive alarm (it is what AMPK reads). Concentrations are relative, total adenylate = 100.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>

  <p class="eeb-foot">Run the first bench and the whole chapter collapses into one sentence: alone, A → B (+12 kJ/mol) has a K'eq near 0.01, so at equilibrium there is about one B for every hundred A; bolt it to ATP hydrolysis and the summed ΔG°' goes to −18.5 — K'eq jumps past 1,000, and the reaction runs. That is all coupling is: arithmetic on ΔG, paid in ATP. The third bench tells you when the cell is willing to pay. It does not spend its last dollar; it holds energy charge near 0.85–0.92, throttling fuel-burning and fuel-building against the same gauge, the way you'd manage a checking account you can never let hit zero.</p>
</figure>

<script>
  const ACCENT = '#0e7c86', NAVY = '#232d4b', ORANGE = '#e57200', GOLD = '#D4A843', FAINT = '#b9b9c2', INK = '#4b4b55';
  const R = 8.314e-3; // kJ/mol·K
  const T = 310; // K
  const ATP_DG = -30.5; // kJ/mol

  const SVGNS = 'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg';
  function el(name: string, attrs: Record<string, string | number>): SVGElement {
    const e = document.createElementNS(SVGNS, name);
    for (const k in attrs) e.setAttribute(k, String(attrs[k]));
    return e;
  }
  const clamp = (v: number, lo: number, hi: number): number => Math.min(hi, Math.max(lo, v));

  type Rung = { name: string; dg: number; currency: boolean };
  const LADDER: Rung[] = [
    { name: 'PEP', dg: -61.9, currency: false },
    { name: '1,3-BPG', dg: -49.3, currency: false },
    { name: 'creatine-P', dg: -43.0, currency: false },
    { name: 'ATP → ADP', dg: -30.5, currency: true },
    { name: 'glucose-6-P', dg: -13.8, currency: false },
    { name: 'glycerol-3-P', dg: -9.2, currency: false },
  ];

  // ---------- MODULE 1: coupling ----------
  // The hill is a quadratic Bézier from (30,132) over a crest to (180,132). The target wagon
  // is one persistent group that is moved with a CSS transform, so coupling visibly hauls it
  // up and over the crest (a transition, switched off under prefers-reduced-motion).
  const HX0 = 30, HX1 = 180, HCX = 105, GROUND = 132;
  function hillPeak(targetDG: number): number { return GROUND - (28 + (targetDG - 5) / 20 * 70) * 2; } // control-point y
  function hillAt(t: number, cy: number): { x: number; y: number; deg: number } {
    const x = (1 - t) * (1 - t) * HX0 + 2 * t * (1 - t) * HCX + t * t * HX1;
    const y = (1 - t) * (1 - t) * GROUND + 2 * t * (1 - t) * cy + t * t * GROUND;
    const dx = 2 * (1 - t) * (HCX - HX0) + 2 * t * (HX1 - HCX);
    const dy = 2 * (1 - t) * (cy - GROUND) + 2 * t * (GROUND - cy);
    return { x, y, deg: (Math.atan2(dy, dx) * 180) / Math.PI };
  }
  function wagon(color: string, label: string, labelFill: string, w: number): SVGElement {
    const g = el('g', {});
    g.appendChild(el('rect', { x: -w / 2, y: -15, width: w, height: 13, rx: 3, fill: color }));
    g.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: -w / 2 + 5, cy: 0, r: 3, fill: NAVY }));
    g.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: w / 2 - 5, cy: 0, r: 3, fill: NAVY }));
    const t = el('text', { x: 0, y: -5.5, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: labelFill, 'font-size': 8, 'font-weight': 700 }); t.textContent = label; g.appendChild(t);
    return g;
  }
  function drawHill(svg: SVGSVGElement, targetDG: number, coupled: boolean): void {
    let layer = svg.querySelector<SVGGElement>('[data-layer]');
    let tw = svg.querySelector<SVGGElement>('[data-target-wagon]');
    if (!layer || !tw) {
      layer = el('g', { 'data-layer': '1' }) as SVGGElement;
      svg.appendChild(layer);
      tw = wagon(ORANGE, 'A→B', '#fff', 28) as SVGGElement;
      tw.setAttribute('data-target-wagon', '1');
      tw.classList.add('eeb-wagon');
      svg.appendChild(tw);
    }
    layer.replaceChildren();
    const cy = hillPeak(targetDG);
    layer.appendChild(el('line', { x1: 8, y1: GROUND, x2: 252, y2: GROUND, stroke: FAINT, 'stroke-width': 1 }));
    layer.appendChild(el('path', { d: `M${HX0} ${GROUND} Q${HCX} ${cy} ${HX1} ${GROUND}`, fill: 'rgba(35,45,75,0.05)', stroke: INK, 'stroke-width': 1.4, 'stroke-opacity': 0.6 }));
    const hl = el('text', { x: HCX, y: GROUND - 8, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: INK, 'font-size': 8 }); hl.textContent = `uphill: +${targetDG} kJ/mol`; layer.appendChild(hl);

    // ATP's own, steeper slope on the right: ATP → ADP + Pi runs downhill by 30.5 kJ/mol
    layer.appendChild(el('path', { d: 'M196 34 L250 130', stroke: ACCENT, 'stroke-width': 1.4, 'stroke-opacity': coupled ? 0.8 : 0.35, fill: 'none' }));
    const sl = el('text', { x: 254, y: 145, 'text-anchor': 'end', fill: ACCENT, 'font-size': 9, opacity: coupled ? 1 : 0.6 }); sl.textContent = 'ATP → ADP + Pi: −30.5'; layer.appendChild(sl);
    // ATP wagon: parked at the top when unlinked, partway down its slope when it is pulling
    const ap = coupled ? { x: 226, y: 88 } : { x: 199, y: 40 };
    const aw = wagon(ACCENT, 'ATP', '#fff', 26);
    aw.setAttribute('transform', `translate(${ap.x} ${ap.y}) rotate(${coupled ? 60.6 : 0})`);
    if (!coupled) aw.setAttribute('opacity', '0.55');
    layer.appendChild(aw);

    const pos = hillAt(coupled ? 0.62 : 0.2, cy);
    tw!.style.transform = `translate(${pos.x}px, ${pos.y}px) rotate(${pos.deg}deg)`;
    if (coupled) {
      // the coupling: a rope over the crest, i.e. the shared intermediate
      layer.appendChild(el('path', { d: `M${pos.x + 10} ${pos.y - 12} Q${(pos.x + ap.x) / 2} ${Math.min(pos.y, ap.y) - 22} ${ap.x - 6} ${ap.y - 10}`, fill: 'none', stroke: GOLD, 'stroke-width': 2 }));
      const bl = el('text', { x: (pos.x + ap.x) / 2 + 4, y: Math.min(pos.y, ap.y) - 20, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: '#7f6315', 'font-size': 9, 'font-weight': 700 }); bl.textContent = 'shared intermediate'; layer.appendChild(bl);
    } else {
      const nl = el('text', { x: pos.x, y: pos.y - 22, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: ORANGE, 'font-size': 9, 'font-weight': 700 }); nl.textContent = 'stalls'; layer.appendChild(nl);
    }
  }

  // ---------- MODULE 2: ladder geometry ----------
  const LAD_TOP = 28, LAD_BOT = 272, LAD_X = 132;
  const rungY = (i: number): number => LAD_TOP + (i / (LADDER.length - 1)) * (LAD_BOT - LAD_TOP);
  function nearestRung(y: number): number {
    let best = 0, bd = Infinity;
    for (let i = 0; i < LADDER.length; i++) {
      const d = Math.abs(y - rungY(i));
      if (d < bd) { bd = d; best = i; }
    }
    return best;
  }
  function drawLadder(svg: SVGSVGElement, tokenIdx: number): SVGCircleElement {
    while (svg.firstChild) svg.removeChild(svg.firstChild);
    // spine
    svg.appendChild(el('line', { x1: LAD_X, y1: LAD_TOP, x2: LAD_X, y2: LAD_BOT, stroke: FAINT, 'stroke-width': 2 }));
    const top = el('text', { x: LAD_X, y: 14, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: INK, 'font-size': 8 }); top.textContent = '↑ stronger donor'; svg.appendChild(top);
    const bot = el('text', { x: LAD_X, y: 290, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: INK, 'font-size': 8 }); bot.textContent = '↓ weaker donor'; svg.appendChild(bot);
    for (let i = 0; i < LADDER.length; i++) {
      const r = LADDER[i], y = rungY(i);
      svg.appendChild(el('line', { x1: LAD_X - 10, y1: y, x2: LAD_X + 10, y2: y, stroke: r.currency ? GOLD : INK, 'stroke-width': r.currency ? 3 : 1.6 }));
      const nm = el('text', { x: LAD_X - 16, y: y - 2, 'text-anchor': 'end', fill: r.currency ? '#7f6315' : NAVY, 'font-size': 9, 'font-weight': r.currency ? 700 : 600 }); nm.textContent = r.name; svg.appendChild(nm);
      const dgt = el('text', { x: LAD_X - 16, y: y + 8, 'text-anchor': 'end', fill: INK, 'font-size': 7.5 }); dgt.textContent = `${r.dg.toFixed(1)} kJ/mol`; svg.appendChild(dgt);
      if (r.currency) { const tag = el('text', { x: LAD_X - 16, y: y + 17, 'text-anchor': 'end', fill: '#7f6315', 'font-size': 7.5, 'font-weight': 700 }); tag.textContent = '◆ the currency'; svg.appendChild(tag); }
    }
    // draggable Pi token at the source rung
    const tok = el('circle', { cx: LAD_X + 30, cy: rungY(tokenIdx), r: 11, fill: ORANGE, stroke: '#fff', 'stroke-width': 2, cursor: 'grab', tabindex: 0, role: 'button', 'aria-label': 'Phosphate token — drag to a rung, or press the down arrow to transfer it to the next lower (spontaneous) rung', 'data-token': '1' }) as SVGCircleElement;
    svg.appendChild(tok);
    const pl = el('text', { x: LAD_X + 30, y: rungY(tokenIdx) + 3, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: '#fff', 'font-size': 8, 'font-weight': 700, 'pointer-events': 'none', 'data-tokenlabel': '1' }); pl.textContent = 'Pi'; svg.appendChild(pl);
    return tok;
  }

  // ---------- MODULE 3: gauge ----------
  function ecAngle(ec: number): number { return Math.PI - clamp(ec, 0, 1) * Math.PI; } // 0->left(π), 1->right(0)
  function gaugePt(ec: number, rad: number): { x: number; y: number } {
    const a = ecAngle(ec);
    return { x: 100 + Math.cos(a) * rad, y: 110 - Math.sin(a) * rad };
  }
  function drawGauge(svg: SVGSVGElement, ec: number): void {
    while (svg.firstChild) svg.removeChild(svg.firstChild);
    const Rr = 78;
    // base arc
    const a0 = gaugePt(0, Rr), a1 = gaugePt(1, Rr);
    svg.appendChild(el('path', { d: `M${a0.x.toFixed(1)} ${a0.y.toFixed(1)} A ${Rr} ${Rr} 0 0 1 ${a1.x.toFixed(1)} ${a1.y.toFixed(1)}`, fill: 'none', stroke: FAINT, 'stroke-width': 8, 'stroke-linecap': 'round' }));
    // green healthy band 0.80–0.95
    const g0 = gaugePt(0.80, Rr), g1 = gaugePt(0.95, Rr);
    svg.appendChild(el('path', { d: `M${g0.x.toFixed(1)} ${g0.y.toFixed(1)} A ${Rr} ${Rr} 0 0 1 ${g1.x.toFixed(1)} ${g1.y.toFixed(1)}`, fill: 'none', stroke: '#2e8b57', 'stroke-width': 8, 'stroke-linecap': 'round', opacity: 0.85 }));
    // tick labels
    [0, 0.5, 1].forEach((v) => { const p = gaugePt(v, Rr + 14); const tt = el('text', { x: p.x, y: p.y + 3, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: INK, 'font-size': 8 }); tt.textContent = v.toFixed(1); svg.appendChild(tt); });
    // needle
    const np = gaugePt(ec, Rr - 6);
    svg.appendChild(el('line', { x1: 100, y1: 110, x2: np.x.toFixed(1), y2: np.y.toFixed(1), stroke: ec < 0.70 ? ORANGE : NAVY, 'stroke-width': 3, 'stroke-linecap': 'round' }));
    svg.appendChild(el('circle', { cx: 100, cy: 110, r: 5, fill: NAVY }));
    const ecl = el('text', { x: 100, y: 126, 'text-anchor': 'middle', fill: ec < 0.70 ? ORANGE : NAVY, 'font-size': 13, 'font-weight': 700, 'font-family': 'monospace' }); ecl.textContent = ec.toFixed(2); svg.appendChild(ecl);
  }

  // ---------- init ----------
  function initBench(root: HTMLElement): void {
    // MODULE 1
    const hillSvg = root.querySelector<SVGSVGElement>('[data-svg="hill"]')!;
    const dgIn = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-in="targetdg"]')!;
    const coupleIn = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-in="couple"]')!;
    const dgOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="targetdg"]')!;
    const dgTargetOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="dg-target"]')!;
    const dgSumOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="dg-sum"]')!;
    const keqOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="keq"]')!;
    const verdictOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="verdict"]')!;
    const SUP: Record<string, string> = { '-': '⁻', '0': '⁰', '1': '¹', '2': '²', '3': '³', '4': '⁴', '5': '⁵', '6': '⁶', '7': '⁷', '8': '⁸', '9': '⁹' };
    const sci = (v: number): string => {
      const [m, e] = v.toExponential(1).split('e');
      return `${m} × 10${String(parseInt(e, 10)).split('').map((c) => SUP[c] ?? c).join('')}`;
    };

    function renderCouple(): void {
      const targetDG = Number.parseFloat(dgIn.value);
      const coupled = coupleIn.checked;
      const sum = coupled ? targetDG + ATP_DG : targetDG;
      const keq = Math.exp(-sum / (R * T));
      dgOut.textContent = `+${targetDG.toFixed(0)}`;
      dgTargetOut.textContent = `+${targetDG.toFixed(1)} kJ/mol`;
      dgSumOut.textContent = `${sum >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${sum.toFixed(1)} kJ/mol`;
      dgSumOut.style.color = sum > 0 ? 'var(--ddp-color-caution)' : 'var(--ddp-color-verified)';
      keqOut.textContent = sci(keq);
      verdictOut.dataset.state = sum > 0 ? 'bad' : 'ok';
      verdictOut.textContent = sum > 0
        ? `Won't go: K'eq < 1, so at equilibrium there is only about 1 B for every ${Math.round(1 / keq).toLocaleString('en-US')} A. Tick the box to couple it to ATP.`
        : `Runs: K'eq ≫ 1, so at equilibrium B outnumbers A about ${Math.round(keq).toLocaleString('en-US')} to 1. Coupling multiplied K'eq by ${sci(Math.exp(-ATP_DG / (R * T)))}.`;
      drawHill(hillSvg, targetDG, coupled);
    }
    dgIn.addEventListener('input', renderCouple);
    coupleIn.addEventListener('change', renderCouple);

    // MODULE 2
    const ladderSvg = root.querySelector<SVGSVGElement>('[data-svg="ladder"]')!;
    const ladderMsg = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="laddermsg"]')!;
    let sourceIdx = 3; // ATP rung
    let tokenEl = drawLadder(ladderSvg, sourceIdx);

    function svgY(evt: PointerEvent): number {
      const pt = ladderSvg.createSVGPoint();
      pt.x = evt.clientX; pt.y = evt.clientY;
      const ctm = ladderSvg.getScreenCTM();
      return ctm ? pt.matrixTransform(ctm.inverse()).y : evt.clientY;
    }
    let dragging = false;
    function moveToken(y: number): void {
      tokenEl.setAttribute('cy', String(clamp(y, LAD_TOP, LAD_BOT)));
      const lbl = ladderSvg.querySelector<SVGTextElement>('[data-tokenlabel]')!;
      lbl.setAttribute('y', String(clamp(y, LAD_TOP, LAD_BOT) + 3));
    }
    ladderSvg.addEventListener('pointerdown', (evt) => {
      const t = evt.target as SVGElement;
      if (t.getAttribute('data-token') === '1') {
        dragging = true;
        ladderSvg.setPointerCapture(evt.pointerId);
        tokenEl.setAttribute('cursor', 'grabbing');
        evt.preventDefault();
      }
    });
    ladderSvg.addEventListener('pointermove', (evt) => { if (dragging) moveToken(svgY(evt)); });
    // Shared transfer decision (used by both drag-drop and keyboard). A transfer is only
    // spontaneous DOWNHILL — to a rung with a less-negative ΔG°' (a weaker phosphoryl donor).
    const nm = (i: number): string => (LADDER[i].currency ? 'ATP' : LADDER[i].name);
    function commit(target: number): void {
      if (target < 0 || target >= LADDER.length || target === sourceIdx) {
        moveToken(rungY(sourceIdx));
        ladderMsg.textContent = target === sourceIdx ? 'Same rung — no transfer.' : 'No rung there.';
        ladderMsg.dataset.state = 'neutral';
      } else if (LADDER[target].dg > LADDER[sourceIdx].dg) {
        moveToken(rungY(target));
        ladderMsg.textContent = `✓ ${nm(sourceIdx)} → ${nm(target)}: spontaneous (ΔG°' = −${Math.abs(LADDER[sourceIdx].dg - LADDER[target].dg).toFixed(1)} kJ/mol). Phosphate moved downhill to a weaker donor.`;
        ladderMsg.dataset.state = 'ok';
        sourceIdx = target;
      } else {
        moveToken(rungY(sourceIdx));
        ladderMsg.textContent = `✕ ${nm(sourceIdx)} → ${nm(target)} is uphill (ΔG°' = +${(LADDER[sourceIdx].dg - LADDER[target].dg).toFixed(1)} kJ/mol): not spontaneous, so the phosphate stays put.`;
        ladderMsg.dataset.state = 'bad';
      }
    }
    function endDrag(evt: PointerEvent): void {
      if (!dragging) return;
      dragging = false;
      tokenEl.setAttribute('cursor', 'grab');
      commit(nearestRung(svgY(evt)));
    }
    ladderSvg.addEventListener('pointerup', endDrag);
    ladderSvg.addEventListener('pointercancel', endDrag);
    // Keyboard path: focus the token, arrow down to transfer to the next lower (spontaneous)
    // rung, arrow up to attempt (and be refused) an uphill move, Home to reset to ATP.
    ladderSvg.addEventListener('keydown', (evt) => {
      const k = evt.key;
      if (k === 'ArrowDown' || k === 'ArrowRight') { commit(sourceIdx + 1); evt.preventDefault(); }
      else if (k === 'ArrowUp' || k === 'ArrowLeft') { commit(sourceIdx - 1); evt.preventDefault(); }
      else if (k === 'Home') { startAt(3); evt.preventDefault(); }
    });
    // Mouse/touch users can only ever move the token down, so give them a way back up.
    function startAt(i: number): void {
      sourceIdx = i; moveToken(rungY(i));
      ladderMsg.textContent = i === 0
        ? 'The phosphate is on PEP, the strongest donor. Now try moving it down to ATP, as glycolysis does.'
        : 'The phosphate is back on ATP. Try moving it down to glucose-6-P, or up to PEP.';
      ladderMsg.dataset.state = 'neutral';
    }
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-start]').forEach((b) => b.addEventListener('click', () => startAt(parseInt(b.dataset.start!, 10))));
    // keep a reference fresh if the SVG is ever redrawn (it isn't after init, but typed-safe)
    tokenEl = ladderSvg.querySelector<SVGCircleElement>('[data-token]')!;

    // MODULE 3
    const gaugeSvg = root.querySelector<SVGSVGElement>('[data-svg="gauge"]')!;
    const atpIn = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-in="atp"]')!;
    const adpIn = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-in="adp"]')!;
    const ampIn = root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-in="amp"]')!;
    const atpOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="atp"]')!;
    const adpOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="adp"]')!;
    const ampOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="amp"]')!;
    const ecOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="ec"]')!;
    const ampkOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="ampk"]')!;
    const cataEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-mode="cata"]')!;
    const anaEl = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-mode="ana"]')!;

    const akrowOut = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-out="akrow"]')!;
    // Adenylate kinase (2 ADP ⇌ ATP + AMP) is modeled as staying at equilibrium,
    // K = [ATP][AMP]/[ADP]², with K fixed by the starting state (85/12/3) and the total
    // adenylate pool held at 100. Dragging ATP re-splits the remainder between ADP and AMP.
    const ATP0 = 85, ADP0 = 12, AMP0 = 3, POOL = ATP0 + ADP0 + AMP0;
    const K_AK = (ATP0 * AMP0) / (ADP0 * ADP0);
    function akSplit(atp: number): { adp: number; amp: number } {
      const rest = POOL - atp;
      if (atp <= 0) return { adp: 0, amp: rest };
      const adp = (-atp + Math.sqrt(atp * atp + 4 * K_AK * atp * rest)) / (2 * K_AK);
      return { adp, amp: rest - adp };
    }
    function renderBattery(fromAtp: boolean): void {
      const atp = Number.parseFloat(atpIn.value);
      if (fromAtp) {
        const sp = akSplit(atp);
        adpIn.value = String(Math.round(sp.adp));
        ampIn.value = String(Math.round(sp.amp));
        akrowOut.textContent = atp < ATP0
          ? `ATP down ${Math.round((1 - atp / ATP0) * 100)}% → AMP up ${(Number(ampIn.value) / AMP0).toFixed(1)}×`
          : '';
      } else {
        akrowOut.textContent = '';
      }
      const adp = Number.parseFloat(adpIn.value);
      const amp = Number.parseFloat(ampIn.value);
      const total = atp + adp + amp;
      const ec = total > 0 ? (atp + 0.5 * adp) / total : 0;
      atpOut.textContent = String(Math.round(atp));
      adpOut.textContent = String(Math.round(adp));
      ampOut.textContent = String(Math.round(amp));
      ecOut.textContent = ec.toFixed(2);
      drawGauge(gaugeSvg, ec);
      const low = ec < 0.70;
      ampkOut.textContent = low
        ? 'Low charge: AMPK on → burn fuel, stop building'
        : ec < 0.85 ? 'Charge slipping below the healthy band'
        : 'High charge: spend on building (anabolic)';
      ampkOut.dataset.state = low ? 'burn' : ec < 0.85 ? 'warn' : 'store';
      // low charge: catabolic ON, anabolic dim; high charge: reverse
      cataEl.dataset.on = low ? '1' : '0';
      anaEl.dataset.on = low ? '0' : '1';
    }
    atpIn.addEventListener('input', () => renderBattery(true));
    adpIn.addEventListener('input', () => renderBattery(false));
    ampIn.addEventListener('input', () => renderBattery(false));

    // static initial render
    renderCouple();
    renderBattery(false);
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-eeb]').forEach(initBench);
</script>

